From 88f1ff5d6630bedc7a748a3d49608c64f15c5b4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Md Arif <111168803+sabamdarif@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 23:11:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] 0041-diagnose-duplicated-rtti-at-backing-catch

Follow-up diagnostic to 0040. The previous run showed:
  - no UNO-RTTI-FABRICATE line  -> the bridge did NOT fabricate a fake
    type_info (0040's fix held; the real symbol was resolvable), yet
  - the typed catch(css::uno::Exception&) in ShowBackingComponent STILL
    missed and control fell through to catch(...).

No fabrication + typed catch still failing means the mismatch is not the
bridge inventing RTTI, but two *real* copies of the same exception
class's type_info living in different .so files. libc++abi compares
type_info by pointer identity, so the thrown object's type_info (from the
library that raised it) is a different address than the copy compiled
into libsofficeapp, and the catch clause does not match.

This patch instruments the catch(...) in Desktop::ShowBackingComponent to
print, via __cxa_current_exception_type(), the in-flight exception's real
mangled class name and type_info pointer, and compares it against this
translation unit's typeid(css::uno::Exception) and
typeid(css::uno::RuntimeException) pointers. The output identifies exactly
which exception class is duplicated, enabling a targeted visibility/linkage
fix (single canonical, default-visibility type_info) rather than more
catch(...) band-aids.

Diagnostic only; no behavior change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 desktop/source/app/app.cxx | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/desktop/source/app/app.cxx b/desktop/source/app/app.cxx
index 455489aa6..2537a283b 100644
--- a/desktop/source/app/app.cxx
+++ b/desktop/source/app/app.cxx
@@ -32,6 +32,12 @@
 #include <cstdlib>
 #include <iostream>
 #include <string_view>
+#if defined(__ANDROID__)
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <typeinfo>
+#include <cxxabi.h>
+#include <com/sun/star/uno/RuntimeException.hpp>
+#endif
 
 #include <app.hxx>
 #include <dp_shared.hxx>
@@ -2860,6 +2866,23 @@ void Desktop::ShowBackingComponent(Desktop * progress)
     }
     catch (...)
     {
+        // DIAGNOSTIC: the typed catch(css::uno::Exception&) above did NOT match,
+        // yet an exception is in flight. Extract its real dynamic type_info so we
+        // can see (a) its true mangled class name and (b) whether its type_info
+        // pointer differs from this library's own copy of the same class -- which
+        // is the signature of duplicated RTTI across .so boundaries.
+        std::type_info * cur = __cxxabiv1::__cxa_current_exception_type();
+        const std::type_info & localUno = typeid(css::uno::Exception);
+        const std::type_info & localRt  = typeid(css::uno::RuntimeException);
+        fprintf(stderr,
+            "RTTI-DIAG: in-flight exception type='%s' ti_ptr=%p | "
+            "local uno::Exception ti_ptr=%p same=%d | "
+            "local uno::RuntimeException ti_ptr=%p same=%d\n",
+            cur ? cur->name() : "(null)", static_cast<void*>(cur),
+            static_cast<const void*>(&localUno),
+            (cur && *cur == localUno) ? 1 : 0,
+            static_cast<const void*>(&localRt),
+            (cur && *cur == localRt) ? 1 : 0);
         fprintf(stderr, "WARNING: ShowBackingComponent caught unknown exception (Bionic RTTI mismatch) - Start Center skipped\n");
         fflush(stderr);
     }
